### Checkout Controller

#### [MODIFY] [CheckoutController.php](file:///c:/wamp64/www/Laravel/eseven-store/app/Http/Controllers/Api/V1/CheckoutController.php)
- In [placeOrder()](file:///c:/wamp64/www/Laravel/eseven-store/app/Services/OrderLifecycleService.php#26-292) response builder: add `checkoutUrl` for tamara/tabby, similar to existing PayPal `redirectUrl` pattern
- Add `tamaraCallback(Request $request)` — handles browser redirect back from Tamara (GET/POST, reads status from query params, redirects to frontend success/failure page)
- Add `tabbyCallback(Request $request)` — same pattern for Tabby

---

### Webhook Controllers

#### [NEW] [TamaraWebhookController.php](file:///c:/wamp64/www/Laravel/eseven-store/app/Http/Controllers/TamaraWebhookController.php)
- Verify notification token from request against stored `payment.tamara_notification_token`
- Handle events: `order_approved` → call `authoriseTamaraOrder()` → mark order paid; `order_declined` → cancel order
- **Idempotent**: check `payment_status` before updating
- Store raw payload in `gateway_payload`, update `gateway_status`
- Record `last webhook received at` in settings

#### [NEW] [TabbyWebhookController.php](file:///c:/wamp64/www/Laravel/eseven-store/app/Http/Controllers/TabbyWebhookController.php)
- Verify custom header matches stored `payment.tabby_webhook_header_name` / `payment.tabby_webhook_header_value`
- Handle events: `authorized` → call `captureTabbyPayment()` → mark order paid; `rejected`/`expired` → cancel order
- Same idempotency and payload-storage pattern

