## Verification Plan

### Automated — Migration & Model
```bash
cd c:\wamp64\www\Laravel\eseven-store
php artisan migrate
```
Verify columns exist:
```bash
php artisan tinker --execute="Schema::hasColumns('orders', ['gateway_order_id','gateway_status','gateway_payload'])"
```

### Manual — Existing Flow Regression (§5 Hard Requirement)
1. Start servers: `php artisan serve` + `npm run dev` (in `/frontend`)
2. Open frontend checkout in browser
3. **COD flow**: Select COD payment → place order → verify order created with `status: pending`, `payment_status: unpaid` in Filament admin
4. **Bank Transfer flow**: Select Bank Transfer → place order → verify same
5. **Stripe flow**: Select Stripe → enter test card `4242424242424242` → verify Payment Element appears → confirm → verify order `status: processing`, `payment_status: paid`
6. Verify each flow reaches the order success page and the order appears in Filament
7. **Admin settings**: Go to Filament → Settings → Payment & Shipping → verify Stripe/COD/Bank sections still work, save, reload, values persist

### Manual — Tamara/Tabby Flows
> [!WARNING]
> Full end-to-end testing of Tamara/Tabby requires **sandbox API keys** which the user must provide. Without keys, we can only verify structural correctness.

1. Enter Tamara/Tabby sandbox credentials in Filament → Payment & Shipping settings
2. Verify the enabled toggles show Tamara/Tabby as checkout options on the frontend
3. Select Tamara → place order → verify redirect to Tamara sandbox → complete → verify redirect back to store with success
4. Verify webhook delivery (use ngrok for local): order transitions to `paid`/`processing`
5. Repeat for Tabby
6. In Filament: verify `gateway_order_id`, `gateway_status`, `gateway_payload` show on order view
7. Test "Sync Status" action — verify it fetches latest status from gateway API

### Manual — Webhook Idempotency
1. After a successful Tamara/Tabby order, manually POST the same webhook payload again
2. Verify order status doesn't change (no double-fulfill)
3. Verify no errors in `storage/logs/laravel.log`
